q q BT 9 TL/F1 7.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 225.8703 25.51181 Tm T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 57.02362 765.8661 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 19 TL/F2 15 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 4 Tm (9. CONCLUSION)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 57.02362 715.8661 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 14 TL/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 32.5 Tm (The Script-Controlled ACL project demonstrates how record-level access can be controlled by evaluating a field)Tj T* (value during authorization. Instead of treating authentication as sufficient for access, the design applies a second)Tj T* (decision layer that checks whether the requested record satisfies the user's permitted conditions.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 57.02362 652.8661 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 14 TL/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 46.5 Tm (The approach provides a flexible foundation for applications where access depends on department, ownership,)Tj T* (project, region, status, or classification. The design also emphasizes secure failure behavior, auditability,)Tj T* (maintainability, and centralized policy enforcement. The resulting system can serve as a prototype for)Tj T* (implementing more advanced attribute-based access control in real applications.)Tj T* ET Q Q

